   "from": "Fundamentals Analyst",
   "to": "Valuation Analyst",
   "section": "funding_valuation",
   "note": "Two figures for your multiples. (1) FY2025 EPS growth of 22.7% is a tax-base artefact: normalising FY2024 at FY2025's 15.6% rate gives net income of $104,222M, so underlying growth was 7.5% and EPS growth 10.4%. Buybacks added 5.4pp of EPS growth FY2023-FY2025 but only 1.9pp in the trailing twelve months; repurchases slowed to $62,094M from $70,579M. (2) No FY2026 10-K or Q4 8-K was on EDGAR at 2026-10-31, so the base is TTM to 2026-06-27: revenue $466,823M, net income $128,930M, EPS $8.72 — 39.5x at $344.63 and a 2.70% FCF yield.",
