{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{
 "url": "https://www.apple.com/leadership/craig-federighi/",
 "title": "Apple Leadership - Craig Federighi - Apple",
 "text": "Craig Federighi is Apple’s senior vice president of Software Engineering, reporting to CEO John Ternus.\nCraig oversees the development of Apple’s software platforms, including iOS, iPadOS, macOS, watchOS, and visionOS. His teams are responsible for delivering the software at the heart of Apple’s innovative products, including the user interface, applications, and frameworks. He also leads Apple’s core AI efforts, including the development of foundation models, applied AI technologies, and the research that powers intelligent experiences across Apple products, including Apple Intelligence and the development of Siri. Craig also leads teams responsible for advancing industry-leading privacy and security protections across Apple’s platforms.\nCraig returned to Apple in 2009 to lead macOS engineering, and in 2012 took on responsibility for iOS as well, delivering all subsequent releases of the world’s most advanced desktop and mobile operating systems.\nPrior to his return, Craig worked at NeXT, followed by Apple, and then spent a decade at Ariba, an e-commerce pioneer where he held several roles, including chief technology officer.\nCraig holds a Master of Science degree in Computer Science and a Bachelor of Science in Electrical Engineering and Computer Science from the University of California, Berkeley.",
 "truncated": false,
 "budget": "7 of 12 used for this brief"
}"}],"isError":false}

{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{
 "url": "https://www.apple.com/leadership/johny-srouji/",
 "title": "Apple Leadership - Johny Srouji - Apple",
 "text": "Johny Srouji is Apple’s chief hardware officer, reporting to CEO John Ternus.\nIn this role, he oversees Apple’s world-class Hardware team, which is responsible for creating and building all of Apple’s hardware products and underlying technologies across a variety of disciplines. Those include product design, system engineering, reliability and durability testing, as well as leading breakthrough technologies in Apple silicon, cellular, displays, cameras, sensors, batteries, and other critical areas of hardware innovation.\nJohny joined Apple in 2008 to lead development of application processors for the iPhone, which became the foundation of Apple silicon that is now at the core of all of Apple’s products.\nPrior to Apple, Johny held senior positions at Intel and IBM in the area of processor development and design. He earned both a bachelor’s and master’s degree in Computer Science from Technion, Israel’s Institute of Technology.",
 "truncated": false,
 "budget": "8 of 12 used for this brief"
}"}],"isError":false}

{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{
 "url": "https://www.apple.com/leadership/eddy-cue/",
 "title": "Apple Leadership - Eddy Cue - Apple",
 "text": "Eddy Cue is Apple’s senior vice president of Services and Health, reporting to CEO John Ternus.\nEddy oversees the full range of Apple’s services, including the App Store, Apple Music, Apple TV, and Apple News, as well as Apple Pay, Apple Card, Maps, Apple Ads, iCloud, and Apple’s productivity and creativity apps. Eddy’s team offers creators and storytellers the opportunity to bring their creative visions to people around the world.\nAs the leader of Apple’s health and fitness teams, Eddy also oversees the company’s health initiatives, pioneering new technologies and advancing medical research to empower people to better understand and manage their health and fitness.\nEddy joined Apple in 1989 and was instrumental in creating the Apple Store online in 1998, the iTunes Store in 2003, and the App Store in 2008. He also played a key role in developing Apple’s award-winning iLife suite of applications.\nEddy earned a bachelor’s degree in Computer Science and Economics from Duke University. He serves on the Board of Trustees of both the Paley Center for Media and Duke University.",
 "truncated": false,
 "budget": "9 of 12 used for this brief"
}"}],"isError":false}

{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{
 "url": "https://www.apple.com/leadership/deirdre-obrien/",
 "title": "Apple Leadership - Deirdre O’Brien - Apple",
 "text": "Deirdre O’Brien is Apple’s senior vice president of Retail + People, reporting to CEO John Ternus.\nAs the leader of Apple’s retail and online teams, Deirdre supports their work to enrich the lives of millions of Apple customers every year. With a laser focus on the connection between customers and the people and processes that serve them, Deirdre and her team create retail experiences that educate and inspire. Deirdre has played an integral role in every Apple product launch throughout her tenure.\nIn her role as the leader of the People team, Deirdre is dedicated to helping everyone at Apple do the best work of their lives, build on the company’s special culture, and achieve their full potential. Her teams foster connections and support employees and leaders across the company, overseeing a diverse range of functions, including Apple University, business partnerships, talent management, recruiting, employee relations, inclusion and diversity, compensation and benefits, and people support & technology.\nDeirdre joined Apple in 1988, and holds a bachelor’s degree in Operations Management from Michigan State University and an MBA from San Jose State University.",
 "truncated": false,
 "budget": "10 of 12 used for this brief"
}"}],"isError":false}

